@@ -0,0 +1,89 @@
+# Pastebin Service
+
+A loopback-only HTTP service for publishing, reading, and withdrawing UTF-8 text snippets, with
+optional lifetimes and file-backed durability.
+
+Requires **Python 3.11 or newer**. No runtime dependencies — the standard library only.
+
+## Run it
+
+```bash
+PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m pastebin serve --port PORT --data DIR
+```
+
+Example:
+
+```bash
+PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m pastebin serve --port 8765 --data ./pastes
+```
+
+The service prints exactly one line once it is listening and ready:
+
+```text
+listening on 127.0.0.1:8765
+```
+
+Nothing else is ever written to standard output; standard error carries only startup failures and
+damaged-storage diagnostics.
+
+| Argument | Required | Accepted | Meaning |
+|----------|----------|----------|---------|
+| `serve`  | yes | the only subcommand | Start the service |
+| `--port` | yes | integer `1`…`65535` | TCP port on `127.0.0.1` |
+| `--data` | yes | filesystem path | Storage directory; created if absent, including parents |
+
+Exit statuses: `0` after a clean interrupt, `1` on a startup failure (port unbindable, storage
+unusable), `2` on an invalid command line.
+
+## Storage
+
+`--data DIR` is the **sole source of truth**. Each snippet is one JSON file at `DIR/<id>.json`,
+written atomically and `fsync`ed before its publication is acknowledged. There is no in-memory
+index and no cache: a later instance started against the same directory reads, serves, and deletes
+everything an earlier instance published, with expiry moments unchanged. Deleting a snippet removes
+its file permanently. The directory is never scanned at startup.
+
+## HTTP API
+
+| Request | Success | Notes |
+|---------|---------|-------|
+| `POST /pastes` with `{"content": "...", "expires_in": 3600}` | `201` with `id`, `delete_token`, `url` | `expires_in` is optional (1…2592000 seconds); absent or `null` means never expires. `content` is at most 65,536 UTF-8 bytes. |
+| `GET /pastes/<id>` | `200` with `id`, `content`, `created_at`, `expires_at` | `delete_token` is never returned here. |
+| `GET /pastes/<id>/raw` | `200` with the text as the whole body | `Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8` |
+| `DELETE /pastes/<id>` with `X-Delete-Token: <token>` | `204` with an empty body | `403` if the token is missing or wrong; `404` if the snippet is unknown or expired, whatever token is presented. |
+
+Every unsuccessful response carries a JSON body of the form `{"error": "..."}`. Timestamps are
+ISO 8601 UTC with second precision and a trailing `Z` (for example `2026-10-23T20:15:00Z`).
+
+```bash
+curl -s -X POST 127.0.0.1:8765/pastes -d '{"content": "hello"}'
+curl -s 127.0.0.1:8765/pastes/$ID
+curl -s 127.0.0.1:8765/pastes/$ID/raw
+curl -si -X DELETE 127.0.0.1:8765/pastes/$ID -H "X-Delete-Token: $TOKEN"
+```
+
+## Tests
+
+`pytest` is the only development dependency:
+
+```bash
+python3 -m pip install -r requirements-dev.txt
+python3 -m pytest            # pytest.ini puts src/ on the path; no PYTHONPATH needed
+python3 -m pytest -q         # terse
+python3 -m pytest -k fr040   # the tests for one requirement
+```
+
+Every functional requirement is named by at least one test; see the requirement-to-test map in
+`specs/001-pastebin-service/data-model.md`.
+
+## Project layout
+
+```text
+src/pastebin/__init__.py   # package marker and version
+src/pastebin/__main__.py   # command line, startup, ready line
+src/pastebin/server.py     # HTTP routing, validation, responses
+src/pastebin/store.py      # snippet records on disk, atomic writes, expiry
+tests/                     # pytest suite, organised by requirement group
+```
+
+Specification, plan, and contracts live in `specs/001-pastebin-service/`.
